@page "/privacy"
@layout Layout.LandingLayout

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy — HrmSystem</PageTitle>

<div class="landing">
    <header class="landing-nav">
        <div class="landing-container landing-nav-inner">
            <a class="landing-brand" href="/">
                <svg width="30" height="21" viewBox="0 0 32 22" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                    <path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd"
                          d="M0.00172773 0V6.85398C0.00172773 6.85398 -0.133178 9.01207 1.98092 10.8388L13.6912 21.9964L19.7809 21.9181L18.8042 9.88248L16.4951 7.17289L9.23799 0H0.00172773Z"
                          fill="#7367F0" />
                    <path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd"
                          d="M7.77295 16.3566L23.6563 0H32V6.88383C32 6.88383 31.8262 9.17836 30.6591 10.4057L19.7824 22H13.6938L7.77295 16.3566Z"
                          fill="#7367F0" />
                </svg>
                <span>HrmSystem</span>
            </a>
            <div class="landing-nav-actions">
                <a class="landing-btn landing-btn-ghost" href="/">Home</a>
                <a class="landing-btn landing-btn-primary" href="login">Sign in</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="landing-section">
        <div class="landing-container" style="max-width: 860px;">
            <h1 class="mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
            <p class="text-muted mb-5">Last updated: July 21, 2026</p>

            <h4>1. Who we are</h4>
            <p>
                HrmSystem is a multi-tenant human-resources platform. Each company that registers
                receives an isolated workspace (a "tenant") in which its HR data is stored and managed.
                This policy explains what personal data the platform processes, why, and what rights
                you have over it.
            </p>

            <h4 class="mt-4">2. Data we collect</h4>
            <p>Depending on how your workspace is used, the platform stores:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Account data</strong> — username, email address, display name, assigned role, and a salted password hash. Plain-text passwords are never stored.</li>
                <li><strong>Employee records</strong> — names, work email addresses, job titles, department membership, hire and termination dates, entered by your workspace administrators.</li>
                <li><strong>Attendance and leave data</strong> — clock-in/clock-out timestamps, leave request dates, types, and approval decisions.</li>
                <li><strong>Messages and announcements</strong> — direct chat messages between workspace members (including read receipts) and company-wide announcements.</li>
                <li><strong>Imported files</strong> — CSV files uploaded by administrators for bulk employee imports, retained only as processing records.</li>
                <li><strong>Technical data</strong> — server logs (IP address, request path, timestamps) used for security, rate limiting, and troubleshooting.</li>
            </ul>

            <h4 class="mt-4">3. How we use your data</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>To operate your company's HR workspace: employee management, attendance, leave approvals, analytics dashboards, announcements, and chat.</li>
                <li>To authenticate you securely (JSON Web Tokens issued at login and kept in your browser's local storage until you sign out).</li>
                <li>To protect the service: login endpoints are rate-limited, and access is scoped by role-based permissions.</li>
                <li>To keep your data safe: automated daily database backups are taken, retained for 7 daily and 4 weekly cycles, then deleted.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>We do not sell personal data, use it for advertising, or share it with third parties.</p>

            <h4 class="mt-4">4. Tenant isolation</h4>
            <p>
                Every record belonging to a company is tagged with that company's tenant identifier and
                is filtered on every read and guarded on every write. Members of one workspace can never
                see or modify data belonging to another workspace.
            </p>

            <h4 class="mt-4">5. Data retention</h4>
            <p>
                Your data is retained for as long as your workspace is active. Terminated employees are
                kept in the record history of the workspace for reporting purposes until the workspace
                administrator removes them. Database backups expire automatically under the retention
                schedule described above.
            </p>

            <h4 class="mt-4">6. Your rights</h4>
            <p>
                You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal data. Employee
                data is controlled by your employer's workspace administrators — direct your request to
                them first; the platform operator will assist with requests the workspace cannot fulfil.
                Workspace data can be exported by administrators in JSON, CSV, or XML formats at any time.
            </p>

            <h4 class="mt-4">7. Cookies and local storage</h4>
            <p>
                The application does not use tracking or advertising cookies. The only browser storage
                used is local storage holding your authentication token for the duration of your session.
            </p>

            <h4 class="mt-4">8. Contact</h4>
            <p>
                For any privacy question or request, contact the platform team at
                <strong>privacy@hrmsystem.example</strong>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="landing-footer">
        <div class="landing-container landing-footer-inner">
            <span>© @DateTime.Now.Year HrmSystem — multi-tenant HR platform</span>
            <span>
                <a href="privacy">Privacy</a> · <a href="terms">Terms</a> · <a href="status">Status</a> · <a href="login">Sign in</a>
            </span>
        </div>
    </footer>
</div>
